    "<span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'>The\n City of Brampton 2023 Fall Orthophoto was captured at 10 cm resolution \nand orthorectified. An orthophoto, orthophotograph or orthoimage is an \naerial photograph geometrically corrected (&quot;orthorectified&quot;) such that \nthe scale is uniform: the photo has the same lack of distortion as a \nmap. Unlike an uncorrected aerial photograph, an orthophotograph can be \nused to measure true distances, because it is an accurate representation\n of the Earth's surface, having been adjusted for topographic relief, \nlens distortion, and camera tilt. - </span><span style='font-family:&quot;Avenir Next W01&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next W00&quot;, &quot;Avenir Next&quot;, Avenir, &quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:16px;'><a href='https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthophoto' style='color:rgb(0, 121, 193); text-decoration-line:none;' target='_blank' rel='nofollow ugc noopener noreferrer'>https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Orthophoto</a></span>"
